# .gitattributes — merge behaviour for APPEND-ONLY ledgers, and nothing else.
#
# docs/audits/impl-estimates.jsonl is written by appending one row per
# (ticket, phase). Two branches that both append produce a textual conflict on
# the last line, and a squash-merge from the queue therefore makes EVERY branch
# carrying the file DIRTY the moment anything merges.
#
# Measured 2026-09-14: it happened to #3001 at ~07:05Z and #3093 at ~08:35Z, 90
# minutes apart, and both resolutions were identical — take the union, main's
# rows first. A resolution that is always the same is a merge driver nobody
# wrote.
#
# `union` is git's built-in driver: both sides' added lines, no markers. Proved
# in a throwaway repo before being written here — without this file the same
# two-sided append leaves 1 conflict marker; with it, 0.
#
# SCOPED DELIBERATELY, AND THE SCOPE IS THE POINT.
# `*.jsonl` would be wrong. Most .jsonl in this repo are GOLDENS and DATASETS —
# crates/aprender-contrastive-data/tests/goldens/*, datasets/*,
# evidence/pr-review/*/receipt.intoto.jsonl. A union merge there silently
# DUPLICATES rows and breaks the byte-identity those files exist to assert. Only
# an append-only ledger may be union-merged, and docs/audits/ is where they live.
#
# scripts/check_append_only_ledgers.sh holds that distinction as a case table.
docs/audits/*.jsonl merge=union
# rex/001 (#4354): the admission files are appended one row per cell, so they are
# ledgers.
docs/audits/rex-001/*.jsonl merge=union
# The corpus (written whole by `rex corpus`) and the #4026 oracle captures (written
# whole by c4026_live.sh) are single-writer goldens, not ledgers: a union merge of
# two regenerations would interleave both versions' rows. Declared `audit-golden`,
# so a two-sided change conflicts and check_append_only_ledgers.sh accepts them.
docs/audits/review-corpus/*.jsonl audit-golden
docs/audits/prm-001/c11-4026-live/*.jsonl audit-golden
# PRM-S1 v2 (#4447): the frozen set and each build's replay rows are written whole
# by `replay build` / `replay run`, so they are single-writer goldens, not ledgers.
docs/audits/prm-001/s1-v2/**/*.jsonl audit-golden
